<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  FISH_BY_BIOME_1 === biome wiring: sets `ZBiome_DesertOasis` (weeping_stones, the true
  pools) fishTypes to recognizability-clean analogs, replacing the vanilla
  Earth-named Fish_Tilapia/Fish_Piranha the donor mod (More Vanilla Biomes)
  ships by default on this def.

  GENERATED by design/Jawa/mods/gen_fish_types.py from the FISH_BY_BIOME_1
  census (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rosters/_fish_candidates.json).
  Do not hand-edit; rerun the generator.

  Donors: freshwater_Common gets the 4 confident swfish_ analogs (Star Wars
  Animal Collection; invented names, no Earth root, clear the sheet's own
  bans on pollution/ambush flavor for a sacred oasis pool). Flat weight 1,
  matching vanilla's own convention where the bucket, not the weight, carries
  the rarity tier.

  FISH_TYPES_PATCH_BUILD_1 (2026-09-10): freshwater_Uncommon TRIMMED to empty
  per the owner's ratified ruling (_fish_assignment_proposal.md §5.2) — the
  4 VCEF_-prefixed secondaries (FrigidSwimmer/Slimefish/Spinyfish/OcularFish)
  are OUT, tonally wrong for the sacred truce pools, and stay benched;
  swfish_Dactopus was considered as a fifth donor and NOT adopted. The bucket
  is explicitly emptied here rather than left unpatched, so the donor mod's
  own vanilla Earth-named default (Fish_Piranha) cannot silently return —
  same "safe no-op for WaterBody.SetFishTypes.TryRandomElement" pattern as
  the sibling SandFishing_CrackedLands.xml used before its own Uncommon
  bucket was filled. The weeping-stones family is 4 species total, v1
  placeholder pending FISH_BESTIARY_COMMISSION_1.

  Only freshwater is touched. `ZBiome_DesertOasis` also carries saltwater_Common/
  Uncommon in the donor's own default def; weeping_stones' roster ruling is a
  standing fresh-water pool with no sea, so saltwater is left as the donor
  mod's own default, untouched, same as the sibling SandFishing_CrackedLands.xml
  pattern (freshwater only) for `ZBiome_Badlands`.

  Wrapped in PatchOperationConditional (checking the target bucket xpath
  exists) rather than a bare PatchOperationReplace, so a shape change in the
  donor def fails the conditional instead of silently matching nothing;
  confirm with validate_patch.py's live-dump and defs-dir checks, since PatchOperationConditional
  and PatchOperationFindMod both report success even on a false condition
  (CLAUDE.md's own warning); the conditional is a defensive shape check, not a
  substitute for validating the actual applied result.

  the_cracked_lands / ZBiome_Badlands is deliberately NOT touched here; the
  other window's SandFishing_CrackedLands.xml (filled by FISH_TYPES_PATCH_BUILD_1)
  already replaces both freshwater buckets and rareCatchesSetMaker on that
  exact def. the_greentide gets its own sibling patch,
  BiomeFishTypes_Greentide.xml, targeting the live BiomeCypreJungle def.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>More Vanilla Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <success>Always</success>
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_DesertOasis"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Common</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_DesertOasis"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Common</xpath>
            <value>
              <freshwater_Common>
                <swfish_Burra MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">1</swfish_Burra>
                <swfish_Daggert MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">1</swfish_Daggert>
                <swfish_Nyork MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">1</swfish_Nyork>
                <swfish_See MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">1</swfish_See>
              </freshwater_Common>
            </value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_DesertOasis"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Uncommon</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_DesertOasis"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Uncommon</xpath>
            <value>
              <freshwater_Uncommon>
              </freshwater_Uncommon>
            </value>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
